        "id": 4
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-02-14T16:45:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Still not in favor of this. It\u0027s not specific to projects and I\u0027d rather it conform to our documented suggestions for roles -- e.g. \"member\".\n\nThere\u0027s no reason why you can\u0027t look for a role named \"member\" and use it if it already exists.\n\nI\u0027m also not sure the role ID needs to be configurable -- it can just be generated randomly as part of the migration.",
      "revId": "ffe7b4f98f1385975fe5407825533c24bcff341b",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAM3/+5i8\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/sql/migrate_repo/versions/017_membership_role.py",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 2218
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-02-15T14:01:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The role id has to be deterministic in order to have a functioning downgrade script.\nWhat if there is is a member role already, and they are using it for different semantics? \n\nIf there is a member role already, we don\u0027t want to remove it in the downgrade script.\n\nIf this process is not determined by preset values, we need to record the values used during the upgrade to figure out what to do during a downgrade.  That seems like madness.\n\nI will make the name of the field configurable, with a default to _member_.  We can document what an end user should be aware of on a migration if they want to use their own role name and id.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAM3/+6ow\u003d",
      "revId": "ffe7b4f98f1385975fe5407825533c24bcff341b",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
